    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0164" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg58"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kimberly to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1891-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                23, 1891</hi>.</date> (Received March 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 253.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Respectfully referring to my No. 239, of
                    January 28, I have the honor to inclose herewith a letter addressed to me by
                    Consul Peterson, at Tegucigalpa, Honduras, bearing upon the subject mentioned in
                    my above-named number.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Samuel Kimberly</hi>.<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad int</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
